@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title init opens on every check and closes on the result
' purpose: what `proveo init` shows before it asks anything, and what it says once it has finished
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_preflight.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_preflight_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_report.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/init_report_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/check_page.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/check_page_test.go
'   the pages between the two ......... _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml
'   what each key means on a page ..... _spec/internal/choiceui/wizard-keys.puml
'   the apply the result reads ........ _spec/internal/ui/step-lines.puml
'   sbx's verdict on the host ......... _spec/internal/sbx/host-readiness.puml
'   the order it landed in ............ _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (W13)
'   the stream's rules (R3) ........... _spec/_plans/output-readability.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS THERE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' init printed its install prerequisites to the stream and listed only the
' FAILED ones in the setup form's header. sbx's own checks (`sbx diagnose`)
' ran after the install, so an operator with sbx already installed learned
' the host was not ready only at the end. A failed blocking prerequisite
' ended init with one error line before any page drew.
' init ended on whatever the last step printed. Nothing said what had been
' answered "later", or what to type next.
'
' ── PAGE 1: EVERY CHECK (W-l) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' A prompted init has four pages now: the checks, setup, credentials,
' operator. The checks page asks nothing. It shows:
'   the title        "init — preparing the <os>/<arch> host"
'   to install sbx   every prerequisite sbx.Prereqs reports, passing ones
'                    included
'   sbx diagnose     every row of `sbx diagnose --json`, when sbx is already
'                    on the host
' Each row carries a mark (passed, warning, failed, skipped), the check's
' name and what it found: Prereq.Detail, or sbx's message. Under a row that
' did not pass come sbx's detail lines, then the fix: Prereq.Fix, or sbx's
' own hint. That is the order of sbx's own `sbx diagnose` table.
' MEASURED 2026-11-11 on sbx 0.50.0: the page drew sbx's detail where the
' message belongs, "SSH client config — ~/.ssh/config:5: Host", and dropped
' the message that says why ("an unmanaged sandbox Host stanza can shadow
' the managed configuration"). The operator could not tell what it meant.
' The payload's two fields: _spec/internal/sbx/host-readiness.puml.
' A FAILING sbx ROW A RUN DOES NOT NEED IS A WARNING here, with one more
' line under its detail: "a run does not need this check; it affects …".
' init's verify step says the same and lets init finish
' (host-readiness.puml, 2026-11-11).
' On a host with no sbx the page holds the install prerequisites alone. On
' macOS that is one row.
' One sentence gives the verdict: "every check passed", or "2 of 7 checks
' need attention". Either way Enter continues to setup: a failing sbx check
' is a reason to reinstall, which setup offers.
' A BLOCKING PREREQUISITE STOPS HERE, ON A PAGE. The verdict reads "blocked:
' nothing good follows an install here: <names>", Enter does nothing, and
' the key line offers Esc alone. Closing the page returns the same error as
' before. With --yes or no terminal the error is still immediate.
' sbx diagnose RUNS ONCE. A step back from setup redraws the rows it got.
' AN sbx THAT DOES NOT ANSWER IS A ROW, NOT A FAILURE: "gave no answer", with
' `proveo init --force` as the fix. The page still continues.
' THE STREAM CARRIES THE PREREQUISITES IN THE sbx BLOCK (R3, 2026-11-11). The
' sbx block prints after the sbx steps (_spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml):
' the "host" fact carries the passing ones dim ("prerequisites met: Apple
' silicon"); an unmet one is an item, × when it blocks the install and ⚠
' otherwise, "<name> — not met", with what it looked for (Prereq.Detail before
' its " — "; the why after it stays in install.go and on the page) and its fix
' dim. The page adds sbx's rows; verify prints those in the result. Until R3
' reportPrereqs printed them under "execution" before the page.
' THE PAGE IS NO FORM. Its Enter word is "continue", not "accept": the e2e
' helpers wait for "enter accept" to find a form.
' Esc on setup now steps back to the checks. It used to end init with
' "cancelled at the init prompt"; that is Esc on the checks page now.
' Golden frames: internal/choiceui/testdata/checks/, 12 files.
'
' ── THE CLOSE: WHAT WAITS, WHAT NEVER RAN, THE VERDICT (R3, 2026-11-11) ────
' The W-m close ("done:" per step, "later: <action> — `<cmd>`", "next:
' `proveo run`") is gone. MEASURED (R3 design, the stubbed tmux harness):
' "done:" lied three ways (a PATH step that added nothing, a git step and a
' GitHub step that ended on ⚠), and five of six closing rows were how-tos
' for answers the operator gave. The operator decided (2026-11-11):
'   F2  how-tos and whys that leave the screen go to `proveo init --help`,
'       the flag help and _spec; init writes NO log file.
'   F3  the readiness verdict prints LAST, in the result.
'   UNREACHED  a separate "not run" fact for what a failure kept from running.
' initRecord collects across every page and every revisit, by the setup
' page's own row labels (sign in · sbx setup · GitHub · git identity ·
' prompt), plus "credentials", "operator name" and "sbx diagnose":
'   ran      each labelled step that did not fail, once
'   later    each row answered "later"; credentials when its page was
'            skipped, or --yes or no terminal kept it from asking
'   not run  the chosen steps after the one that failed, and the pages a
'            failure or a run blocker kept init from reaching
' EVERY PAGE THAT FAILS NAMES THE PAGES AFTER IT (initRecord.pages): setup,
' credentials or operator, through a step, a form that cannot draw, or a
' Ctrl+C in a sign-in, whose answered rows after it list too. A quit, a
' cancel and a blocked prerequisite are the operator's or end before the
' result, so they list nothing. A distro package the release does not ship
' fails the install step itself, so the steps after it list as for any step.
' A label already "later" (the credentials page skipped, then a failure on
' a revisit of setup) stays "later" alone: one list per label.
' An action that ran on an earlier visit never lists as later.
' A row a revisit chooses "now" leaves "later" (leaveUnchosen), so a failure
' before it runs lists it under "not run" (the second R3 review: "later:
' sign in" printed above "⚠ init — stopped at sign in").
' "leave as is" on the network baseline is no "later": nothing waits.
' initReport.close prints what an early end left unprinted (sbx, git,
' credentials, operator), then ONE results block:
'   ● later:   GitHub                 one Facts block; each list stacked
'              git identity           under its key (P3)
'   ● not run: credentials            only after a failure or a run blocker
'   ⚠/× each failing sbx check, its evidence and hint dim
'   one closing line, the verdict:
'     ✓ host — ready to run                    verify found nothing a run needs
'     × host — not ready to run                a run blocker; exit 1
'     ⚠ init — quit at page n/N                a confirmed quit; exit 1; dim
'                                              "host ready to run" when verify
'                                              reached that verdict
'     ⚠ init — cancelled at the checks page    or "the setup page"; exit 1
'     ⚠ init — stopped at <row>                a program init handed the
'                                              terminal to failed (sbx login,
'                                              the installer, the package,
'                                              gh auth login): its own error
'                                              stands; exit 1; after a
'                                              Ctrl+C, dim "Ctrl+C ended it"
'                                              and proveo dies of SIGINT
'                                              (status 130)
'     × <row> — failed                         a failure proveo found itself
'                                              (a download, a digest, a prefix
'                                              it cannot write); the error dim
'     × init — stopped                         an error no step names: the
'                                              setup page's own form error, or
'                                              no plan for a prefix it chose;
'                                              the error dim; exit 1
'   none when verify gave no answer: its ⚠ item is the last line.
' THE VERDICT STAYS LAST (F3, the second R3 review): after a verify that
' found the host ready, every ending but success keeps "host ready to run"
' as its last dim line, under the error or "Ctrl+C ended it" when there is
' one; until then only a quit or a cancel kept it.
' Each ending but success returns backend.Reported (or a re-raised Stopped),
' so main prints nothing more: one × host line, never main's "× host not
' ready to run: <names>" under it. A blocked prerequisite ends on its × item in the
' sbx block and prints no result. Errors before any block exists (no home
' and no --prefix, no temp dir, no build for this host) keep main's ×.
' THE RESULT IS PRINTED, NOT PAGED: a page takes its text with it.
' MOVED TO `proveo init --help` (F2): what "later" rows need ("`proveo init`
' again offers what was left for later; `sbx login` and `sbx setup` run
' sbx's own"), "Then `proveo run` lists the harnesses this host can start",
' "proveo does not manage the host … --force", `source <rc>`, the prompt
' kit's "open a new shell" and its icon preset. NOT CHOSEN: an init log
' file (F2 b); dim how-tos under every "later" row (F2 c, against the
' HOW-TO decision).
'
' ── WHAT RAN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' macOS and linux/arm64, on tmux against the stub sbx: the checks page shows
' both groups and no "enter accept"; Esc on setup returns to it and Enter
' goes on without re-running sbx login or sbx setup; the result lists what
' ran as done, what was skipped as later with its command, and the next
' command. The eight older init tests pass through one changed helper,
' which continues past the checks page.
' 2026-11-11: the stub sends sbx 0.50.0's shape, one row with a warning; the
' page shows its message, its detail and its hint (macOS, tmux).
' 2026-11-11: the stub also fails "SSH client config". Every init test
' finishes, and the result lists "done: verify sbx". With RunBlockers swapped
' back to every failed row, the checks test failed on "host not ready to
' run: SSH client config" (macOS, tmux).
' NOT RUN: a blocked host. The blocked page is unit-tested and drawn in the
' golden frames; no test host fails a blocking prerequisite.
' NOT RUN: a host without sbx, so the one-row page drew in no test.
'
' R3 (2026-11-11, the stubbed harness, macOS): every init e2e passes with
' the anchors the plan's E2E ANCHORS THAT MOVE (R3) lists.
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/init_preflight_test.go:
'   TestThePreflightRowsCarryEveryCheckWithItsStateAndItsFix
'   TestAHostWithoutSbxShowsOnlyWhatInstallingNeeds
'   TestAnSbxThatDoesNotAnswerIsARowAndNotAnError
'   TestAnSbxRowShowsItsMessageAndKeepsItsDetailAsEvidence
'   TestAFailingCheckARunDoesNotNeedIsAWarningThatSaysWhatItAffects
'   TestOnlyAFailingCheckARunNeedsFailsInit
'   TestTheResultLeavesOutAnActionThatRanOnAnEarlierVisit
'   TestSignInLeftForLaterUsesTheSetupPagesRowNames
'   TestAFailureNamesWhatItKeptFromRunningApartFromLater
'   TestARowAnsweredLaterIsNeverAlsoNotRun
'   TestAFailedPageNamesThePagesAfterIt
'   TestARowChosenNowOnARevisitLeavesLater
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/init_report_test.go:
'   TestEveryEndingAfterAPassedVerifyKeepsTheVerdictLast
'   TestAnErrorWithNoStepClosesOnInitStopped
'   TestAFailedGhAuthLoginEndsInitOnWhereItStopped
'   TestACredentialsPageStopNamesWhatItKeptFromRunning
'   TestAMissingDistroPackageStopsAtTheInstallAndNamesWhatNeverRan
'   TestTheSbxBlockNamesAnotherSbxThisShellsPathFindsFirst
'   TestTheResultListsWhatWaitsAndClosesOnTheVerdict
'   TestARunBlockerClosesOnOneHostVerdictAndNamesWhatNeverRan
'   TestAQuitClosesOnOneWarningWithTheVerdictDim
'   TestAHandOffFailureEndsOnWhereInitStopped
'   TestACtrlCDuringAHandOffEndsInitCleanlyWith130
'   TestAFailureProveoFoundClosesOnItsStep
'   TestABlockedPrerequisiteEndsOnItsItem
'   TestARevisitPrintsOneReadinessSetAndItsSbxLinesUnderSbx
'   TestTheCredentialsBlockPrintsOnceFromTheLatestPass
'   TestFlagHelpCarriesTheHowTosThatLeftTheScreen
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/check_page_test.go:
'   TestTheCheckPagesKeys
'   TestTheCheckPageShowsEveryCheckItsMarkAndTheHintUnderOneThatFailed
'   TestWhatACheckFoundDrawsUnderARowThatDidNotPassAboveItsHint
'   TestABlockedCheckPageSaysWhyAndOffersNoWayOn
'   TestAShortCheckPageScrollsAndKeepsItsVerdictAndItsKeys
'   TestTheCheckPageMatchesItsGoldenFrames
' Pinned by e2e/init_steps_test.go:
'   TestInitOpensOnTheChecksAndClosesOnTheResult
'   TestInitOnAReadyHostClosesOnReady
'   TestInitARunBlockerClosesOnTheHostVerdict
'   TestInitCtrlCInSbxsWizardEndsOnWhereItStopped

component "install prerequisites\nsbx.Prereqs" as PRE <<data>>
component "sbx diagnose\nwhen sbx is on the host" as DIAG <<cloud>>
component "page 1 · the checks\nevery row, with its mark" as PAGE <<app>>
component "**a blocking prerequisite**\nEnter does nothing" as BLOCK <<error>>
component "setup · credentials · operator" as PAGES <<app>>
component "initRecord\nran · later · not run" as REC <<data>>
component "the result\nlater · not run · checks · verdict" as RESULT <<host>>

PRE ARROW_MAIN PAGE
DIAG ARROW_OPTIONAL PAGE
PAGE ARROW_MAIN PAGES : Enter
PAGE ARROW_ERROR BLOCK
PAGES ARROW_MAIN REC : each step that ran, each answer "later"
REC ARROW_MAIN RESULT

note bottom of PAGE
  **It asks nothing.** Passing checks show too,
  and sbx's own rows join them when sbx is
  already installed. A row that did not pass
  carries what was found and its fix.
end note

note bottom of BLOCK
  **Stopped on a page, not by a line.** The
  verdict names the prerequisite and the key
  line offers Esc alone. Without a terminal
  the old error is still immediate.
end note

note bottom of REC
  **A revisit cannot undo a step that ran.**
  A revisit opens every one-shot action on
  "later"; the record remembers the sign-in
  that ran, so "later" never lists it.
end note

note bottom of RESULT
  **It ends on the verdict.** What waits, what
  a failure kept from running, the checks sbx
  failed, then one closing line: ✓ or × host,
  or ⚠ where init stopped.
end note

note bottom of DIAG
  **Asked once.** The rows are kept for the
  whole init. A sbx that gives no answer is
  one warning row with the reinstall command,
  and the wizard goes on.
end note
@enduml
